[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0m[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what was changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation had [1mthree bugs[22m in the [38;5;10mmain()[0m function's input handling, all stemming from behavioral differences between C's [38;5;10mfgets[0m/[38;5;10msscanf[0m and Rust's [38;5;10mBufRead::lines()[0m/[38;5;10mstr::parse()[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: Integer parsing was too strict[0m[0m
- **C behavior**: [38;5;10msscanf(input, "%d", &choice)[0m extracts only the leading integer from a string. Input like [38;5;10m"1,2,3"[0m successfully parses as [38;5;10m1[0m.[0m[0m
- **Rust behavior**: [38;5;10mline.trim().parse::<i32>()[0m requires the [3mentire[23m string to be a valid integer. [38;5;10m"1,2,3"[0m fails to parse, producing "Invalid input" instead of running demo 1.[0m[0m
- **Affected tests**: [38;5;10mcomma[0m, [38;5;10mcolon[0m, [38;5;10msemicolon[0m, [38;5;10mperiod[0m, [38;5;10mhyphen[0m, [38;5;10mdecimal_number[0m, [38;5;10mspace_between_digits[0m, [38;5;10mscientific_notation[0m, [38;5;10mhex_like_input[0m, [38;5;10mcommand_injection_like[0m, [38;5;10msql_injection_like[0m, and many others (22 tests).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: No line-length limit[0m[0m
- **C behavior**: [38;5;10mfgets(input, 256, stdin)[0m reads at most 255 bytes. A 1000-character line gets split into 4 separate reads, each processed as a separate menu input.[0m[0m
- **Rust behavior**: [38;5;10mBufRead::lines()[0m reads the entire line regardless of length, so a 1000-char line is processed as a single input.[0m[0m
- **Affected test**: [38;5;10mvery_long_input_line[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 3: Integer overflow handling[0m[0m
- **C behavior**: [38;5;10msscanf("%d")[0m with [38;5;10m2147483648[0m (INT_MAX+1) returns success (1) and stores a wrapped value, hitting the [38;5;10mdefault: printf("Invalid choice")[0m branch.[0m[0m
- **Rust behavior**: [38;5;10mparse::<i32>()[0m returns [38;5;10mErr[0m on overflow, producing "Invalid input" instead of "Invalid choice".[0m[0m
- **Affected test**: [38;5;10minteger_overflow[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### The fix[0m[0m
Added two helper functions to [38;5;10mmain()[0m:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfgets_256()[0m: reads raw bytes up to 255 at a time, stopping at [38;5;10m\n[0m, emulating C's [38;5;10mfgets(buf, 256, stdin)[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msscanf_int()[0m: skips leading whitespace, extracts the leading sequence of digits (with optional sign), parses as [38;5;10mi64[0m, then truncates to [38;5;10mi32[0m — matching C's [38;5;10msscanf("%d")[0m semantics including overflow wrapping[0m[0m
